    description: "Found 2026-10-27 by the INV-nuzas re-check, production `hypergumbo survey` on dev 8c61dbe07c (fixtures in the session scratchpad, nuzas_recheck/js and ctl_js). WI-rilof (#1877/#1879) resolved the shape it was filed on (`const { helper } = require('@ws/b'); helper()`, and the ESM named import `import { shout } from '@ws/c'; shout()`); three other import shapes of a workspace sibling still call a tier-3 phantom.\n\nnpm workspace (root package.json workspaces [\"packages/*\"]; @ws/b = packages/b, @ws/c = packages/c with a TS entry), production code in packages/a/src:\n1. module object of a require: `const b = require('@ws/b'); b.helper()` -> calls `javascript:@ws/b:0-0:helper:external_symbol` (ast_method_inferred)\n2. namespace import: `import * as C from '@ws/c'; C.shout(\"b\")` -> calls `typescript:@ws/c:0-0:shout:external_symbol`\n3. default import: `import cDefault from '@ws/c'; cDefault()` (c exports `export default function cDefault`) -> calls `typescript:@ws/c:0-0:default:external_symbol`\nControl (ctl_js): the same three shapes against RELATIVE imports (`require('./b')`, `from './c'`) all resolve to the real functions, so the gap is the package-name route WI-rilof added only for named bindings.\n\nTwo more phantoms appear with relative imports too, so they are general JS/TS behaviour; in a workspace they carry the @ws/ prefix. Decide with this item whether they are acceptable stand-ins:\n4. `new b.Engine()` emits a module_attr_ref to `javascript:@ws/b:0-0:@ws/b.Engine:external_symbol` (relative: `./b.Engine`) BESIDE the correct instantiates edge to class Engine.\n5. every import emits an imports edge to a `<spec>:0-0:module` external_symbol stand-in BESIDE the real file edge (`javascript:@ws/b:0-0:module`, `typescript:@ws/c:0-0:module`, `javascript:@ws/b/src/util/deep:0-0:module`).\nShapes 1-3 are consumer-reached phantoms with an in-tree definition: INV-nuzas counterexamples. Closure: the fixture through the production survey, shapes 1-3 landing on the real nodes, plus the relative-import control unchanged."  # 6f74
